 "text": "The gruagach is a Scottish fairy being who watches over cattle like a barnyard brownie. She asked for milk poured into hollow stones and dressed in green with long golden hair. Even on fine days she looked soaked and would ask those she met if she could dry by the fire. A small man with long red hair could also appear and take over the farm work.",
 "okr": {
  "objective": "Present the gruagach as the fairy keeper of Scottish herds.",
